WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
And after going a long way around in search of truth,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.800
we finally realize that someone has spoken it.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.700
That person is familiar to us,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.200
yet somehow not well known to us.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.200
Everyone mentions him, yet we often reject him.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.200
In our culture, background and country, he can seem far away.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.200
His name is Jesus.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.700
I grew up in a traditional family.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.200
We worshipped idols from childhood.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.200
The Buddha statue in our home was imported from India.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.700
I worshipped earnestly.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.200
So “believing in Jesus” felt foreign to us. We even resisted it.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.700
We used to say, “Eat your fill; when you die, no one will be there for you.”

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.700
“Believe in Jesus? Nothing good will come of it.”

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:57.200
But the Lord’s steadfast love found so many ways

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:03.200
to use different circumstances to bring us to the end of ourselves.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.700
There is a saying: “When we reach our end, God’s work begins.”

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:17.200
It is remarkable how life can take us around in a circle,

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:23.200
until we see our limits and what we cannot reach on our own,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:30.700
and then begin to ask: Is there One without limits, who knows all, is everywhere, and can do all things?

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:42.200
Could this One hold all things, explain them, and tell us where everything began and where it is going?

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:52.200
Could there be a Creator and Ruler who holds all things

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.200
and can tell us how it all came to be?

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:06.200
Many people hope for this. Mr. Dongfang Bai said life has three aims: first, to seek the Way and truth;

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:14.200
second, to live out the truth we seek; and third, to share the truth we live.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:21.200
Even Confucius said, “If I hear the Way in the morning, I can die content that evening.”

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:31.200
To hear the truth in the morning and die that evening would still be worthwhile, because he had found a place to stand and live.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:38.500
But what is the Way they sought? Can it truly give us a sure foundation for life?
